  "step": [
    {
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 1,
      "name": "Step 1",
      "text": "Achieving that super smooth, professional look on your interior trim isn't rocket science, but it definitely requires a good process. Here's a quick rundown of how the pros often tackle it:"
    },
    {
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 2,
      "name": "Step 2",
      "text": "Step 1: Clean and Vacuum Thoroughly. Before anything else, get that trim sparkling clean. Dust, grime, and cobwebs are enemies of a smooth paint job. A good wipe-down and vacuuming ensure you're working with a clean slate."
    },
    {
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 3,
      "name": "Step 3",
      "text": "Step 2: Scuff Sand and Repair. Don't skip the sanding! A light scuff sand creates a surface that paint can really grip onto. While you're at it, inspect for any gaps or imperfections. Now's the time to fill those in and make any repairs."
    },
    {
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 4,
      "name": "Step 4",
      "text": "Step 3: Prime if Necessary. If you're painting over a dark color with a lighter one, or if you're dealing with bare wood or old oil-based paint, a quality primer is your best friend. It helps with adhesion and ensures an even finish."
    },
    {
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 5,
      "name": "Step 5",
      "text": "Step 4: Apply Finish Coats. Once the primer is dry, it's time for your finish coats. Typically, two thin coats are better than one thick one. Make sure to allow proper drying time between each coat. Often, trim is painted before walls, so any overlap can be cleaned up during wall painting."
    },
    {
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 6,
      "name": "Step 6",
      "text": "Following these steps can really elevate the look of your trim. If it feels like too much, or if your trim has a lot of existing issues, bringing in a team like HH Remodeling LLC can save you time and headaches, making sure the job gets done right."
    }
  ],
